THOUGHT: The error is that `center` (and also `right`/`left`) are considered nullable when dereferenced. These are taken from `stack` and `parent` fields, which are nullable in general, but in this specific balancing loop they are only used when the stack has the expected shape. To satisfy NullAway for just the `center` dereference, I can add explicit null checks (and throw if violated) before dereferencing `right.parent` and `center.parent`. This preserves behavior (these cases should never be null if the algorithm is correct) while giving NullAway proof of non-nullness. I’ll edit the file to introduce local variables with null checks around the problematic lines, then later run the build to confirm the error count drops by one.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/gson && sed -i '724,732s/Node<K, V> right = stack;/Node<K, V> right = stack;
	          if (right == null) {
	            throw new IllegalStateException("Right node on stack is null");
	          }/;724,732s/Node<K, V> center = right.parent;/Node<K, V> center = right.parent;
	          if (center == null) {
	            throw new IllegalStateException("Center node is null");
	          }/;724,732s/Node<K, V> left = center.parent;/Node<K, V> left = center.parent;
	          if (left == null) {
	            throw new IllegalStateException("Left node is null");
	          }/' gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/internal/LinkedHashTreeMap.java
```

